  "reasoning": "Cook Political Report\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index rates Oklahoma at roughly R+17, indicating the state votes about 17 points more Republican than the national average in recent presidential elections.[1][12] In the 2020 presidential election, Republicans received about 65.4% of the vote in Oklahoma versus roughly 33.8% for Democrats, a margin of about 31.6 points, and similar landslide margins have recurred across recent cycles.[9][13] I could not find any 2026 federal head\u2011to\u2011head polling or forecaster ratings within the last 45 days tied to named candidates, so this assessment relies on those consistently lopsided prior results as a structural baseline, which strongly indicate a solid Republican lean absent evidence of a major realignment.[3][9][13]",
